From 17d2f70292d506882755f3799a1d1fa9e8ac9527 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:40:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(nethernet): update native binding to avoid exit deadlocks

The September libdatachannel bundle can deadlock when the JVM exits during a data-channel callback. C++ static registry destruction waits for a callback mutex after Java callbacks have stopped.

Use the October 29 bundle already consumed by the Bedrock add-on. Its C API registries have process lifetime and retain explicit rtcCleanup support, so process exit does not destroy active channels on the halted VM thread.

The published Java and native artifacts match their advertised SHA-256 checksums. Their source chain is libdatachannel-java 6be4ad71e1f10dc56a09af6daeac0e1122e23e7a, libdatachannel 3db103e248d7aeb2d7c48da29f0c0f82efd2cadd, and libjuice 67bfe8903b8d6a5dcf8d731271aec68257cb2872.

A real loopback callback-overlap probe hangs with the previous bundle and exits normally with the new bundle on Linux with JDK 17 and 25. Explicit peer-close and awaited-close controls still pass. Other native platforms require their own runtime verification.

Pin the Java facade and native bundle to the same immutable Maven publication. Exclude the facade from NetherNet using its group and module separately, and from the bundle before adding the explicit matching facade. The previous colon-delimited exclusion did not remove NetherNet's older facade, which could be packaged beside newer JNI binaries.
---
 build.gradle | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build.gradle b/build.gradle
index 43f58fd2d47bc0651d37a6245d0321c5a3bd7701..c8caaf07192f821e3fdf0e59ef78c619fac5eb47 100644
--- a/build.gradle
+++ b/build.gradle
@@ -119,9 +119,13 @@ dependencies {
     includeInJar("org.cloudburstmc.netty:netty-transport-nethernet:2.0.0.CR4-20261001.235918-13") {
         exclude group: "io.netty"
         exclude group: "org.bouncycastle"
-        exclude group: "dev.opencollab:libdatachannel-java"
+        exclude group: "dev.opencollab", module: "libdatachannel-java"
+    }
+    def libDataChannelVersion = "0.24.6.0-20261029.091642-10"
+    includeInJar "dev.opencollab:libdatachannel-java:$libDataChannelVersion"
+    includeInJar("dev.opencollab:libdatachannel-java-arch-detect:$libDataChannelVersion") {
+        exclude group: "dev.opencollab", module: "libdatachannel-java"
     }
-    includeInJar "dev.opencollab:libdatachannel-java-arch-detect:0.24.6.0-20260930.214316-2"
     includeInJar "gs.mclo:api:6.2.1"
     includeInJar "net.lenni0451:optconfig:1.1.1"
 
